e":"text-xl font-display font-bold text-slate-900 group-hover:text-brand-blue transition-colors","children":"Finance-Led Approach"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed","children":"Our leadership team includes Chartered Accountants and finance veterans. We understand your finance processes as deeply as the technology â€” preventing costly post-go-live fixes."}]]}],["$","div","2",{"className":"p-8 rounded-[28px] bg-white border border-slate-200/90 shadow-sm space-y-4 group hover:border-brand-blue/30 hover:shadow-lg transition-all","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"block text-sm font-mono font-bold tracking-widest text-brand-blue/70","children":"03"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-xl font-display font-bold text-slate-900 group-hover:text-brand-blue transition-colors","children":"Fixed-Scope Commitment"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed","children":"We commit to a defined scope, timeline, and cost upfront. No creep, no surprises â€” a signed Statement of Work that protects you from day one."}]]}],["$","div","3",{"className":"p-8 rounded-[28px] bg-white border border-slate-200/90 shadow-sm space-y-4 group hover:border-brand-blue/30 hover:shadow-lg transition-all","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"block text-sm font-mono font-bold tracking-widest text-brand-blue/70","children":"04"}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-xl font-display font-bold text-slate-900 group-hover:text-brand-blue transition-colors","children":"Deep ABAP Expertise"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed","children":"Our consultants adapt, not abandon, your custom code. Proven ABAP remediation methodology means your Z-programs and exits continue working on S/4HANA."}]]}],"$L45","$L46"]}]]}]}]
24:["$","section",null,{"data-theme":"light","className":"py-16 sm:py-24 lg:py-32 bg-white border-b border-slate-200/80","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-3xl mb-12 sm:mb-16 text-center mx-auto","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-4","children":["$","span",null,{"className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3.5 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-bold tracking-wider uppercase border bg-blue-50 text-brand-blue border-blue-100","children":"Frequently Asked Questions"}]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight leading-[1.15] mb-5 text-slate-900","children":["Your questions, ",["$","span",null,{"className":"text-brand-blue","children":"answered honestly"}],"."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mx-auto text-slate-600","children":"Clear, upfront answers on Brownfield migration timelines, historical data preservation, custom ABAP code, and post go-live support."}]]}],["$","$L47",null,{"items":[{"id":1,"question":"What is the difference between Brownfield and Greenfield migration?","answer":"Brownfield (System Conversion) converts your existing SAPÂ® ECC system to S/4HANA in-place. All historical data, custom code, configurations, and organisational structures are carried forward. Greenfield is a completely fresh implementation where everything is rebuilt from scratch. Brownfield is faster, cheaper, and far less disruptive â€” making it the right choice for most organisations that have a mature, working ECC system. Greenfield makes sense only when a company wants to completely re-engineer their processes or has a very simple ECC landscape."},{"id":2,"question":"Is 16 weeks really achievable? What are the conditions?","answer":"Yes â€” for well-scoped, mid-market ECC systems with a focused core (FI/CO, MM, SD, PP). The 16-week timeline applies when the ECC landscape is reasonably clean, custom code volume is manageable, client resources are available for UAT and workshops, and there are no external dependencies (e.g. waiting for third-party vendor APIs). We perform a free readiness assessment before confirming your timeline. Complex multi-company, multi-country, or highly customised landscapes may require 20â€“28 weeks. We will tell you the honest timeline at the assessment stage."},{"id":3,"question":"Will I lose any data during migration?","answer":"No. Brownfield migration converts the entire database â€” all transactional data, historical records, master data, and documents carry forward unchanged. We perform multiple validation checks and reconciliations throughout the process, and our cutover runbook includes a formal data integrity sign-off. Selective data archiving (of aged open items) may be recommended as a best practice before cutover, but this is always a client decision â€” nothing is deleted without your explicit approval."},{"id":4,"question":"Which versions of SAPÂ® ECC are supported for brownfield migration?","answer":"SAPÂ® supports brownfield migration from ECC 6.0 EHP 6 and above (EHP 7 and EHP 8 are the most common). If you are on an older EHP, we typically perform an upgrade to EHP 7/8 as a pre-step. Being on a recent support package level also reduces the number of pre-processing steps. Our assessment phase will confirm your exact starting point and identify any prerequisite steps before the main conversion."},{"id":5,"question":"What happens to my custom ABAP code and Z-programs?","answer":"Custom code does not automatically work on S/4HANA without review. We run SAPÂ®'s Custom Code Migration Workbench during the assessment phase to identify all impacted programs. Most custom code can be adapted to work correctly on S/4HANA with minor to moderate changes (typically syntax corrections and adaptation to new S/4HANA data models). We include custom code remediation in our fixed-scope package up to an agreed number of objects. Code that cannot be adapted is flagged early so you can make informed decisions."},{"id":6,"question":"How much system downtime is required at go-live cutover?","answer":"Brownfield conversion requires a production downtime window â€” typically 24â€“48 hours depending on database size and system complexity. We schedule this over a weekend or public holiday to minimise business impact. Our cutover simulation in Phase 4 rehearses the exact steps so we know the downtime to the minute before the actual go-live. We aim to reduce downtime through careful pre-processing, parallel preparation, and optimised conversion scripts run during the pre-go-live window."},{"id":7,"question":"Will my staff need extensive retraining?","answer":"No â€” and this is one of the major advantages of brownfield. Business processes, transaction codes, and workflows remain largely the same. The main change for end users is the new SAPÂ® Fiori user interface, which is more modern and intuitive than the classic SAPÂ® GUI. We include role-based Fiori orientation training and key user sessions in our package. Most users are productive within a few days of go-live. There is no need to re-learn core business processes from scratch."},{"id":8,"question":"What specific business benefits does S/4HANA deliver over ECC?","answer":"S/4HANA delivers significant improvements: Real-time analytics and reporting directly in the system (no separate BW required for standard reports), a simplified Finance data model (Universal Journal) that eliminates reconciliation effort, faster period-end close, embedded AI and predictive analytics, SAPÂ® Fiori for a modern user experience on any device, tighter integration across modules, and a platform ready for SAPÂ® BTP extensions. Most clients see measurable improvements in month-end close time and finance reporting speed within the first quarter after go-live."},{"id":9,"question":"How is XpmindGlobal able to offer ~40% cost savings?","answer":"The ~40% cost saving is achieved through three factors: (1) Our offshore delivery model means you get senior consultants at lower blended rates without compromising quality, (2) Our proprietary accelerator toolkit â€” pre-built templates, test scripts, and automation â€” reduces the hours required by 30â€“40% compared to building everything from scratch, and (3) Fixed-scope engagements mean we have refined our delivery to eliminate waste. We are not adding junior staff to pad hours; our senior-led model is efficient and outcome-focused."},{"id":10,"question":"What support do you provide after go-live?","answer":"We include 4 weeks of dedicated Hypercare support as part of the migration package â€” a dedicated support team, daily status calls, and priority resolution of any production issues. After Hypercare, we offer a structured transition to our Application Management Services (AMS) model, where the same team that did your migration continues supporting your S/4HANA system. This ensures zero knowledge transfer overhead and continuity of care. Our AMS contracts are month-to-month with no lock-in."}],"theme":"light"}]]}]}]
25:["$","section",null,{"data-theme":"dark","children":["$","$L48",null,{"eyebrow":"Limited Capacity â€” Project Slots Filling Fast","headline":"Ready to move to S/4HANA? Let's assess your system â€” free.","subtitle":"A 90-minute readiness session with our SAPÂ® experts. We'll assess your ECC landscape, identify risks, and give you an honest timeline and cost estimate â€” no obligation.","buttonText":"Book Free Assessment â†’","defaultService":"S/4HANA Upgrade & Migration"}]}]
